---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import {
  personSchema,
  breadcrumbSchema,
  pageSchema,
} from '../../lib/schema';

const crumbs = [
  { label: 'About', href: '/about/' },
  { label: 'Jordan Ellis, LPC' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Jordan Ellis, LPC | Madison Counselor"
  description="Meet Jordan Ellis, the fictional counselor created for the Align Therapy Group design demonstration."
  schema={pageSchema([
    personSchema('/about/jordan-ellis/'),
    breadcrumbSchema(crumbs, Astro.url.pathname),
  ])}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Clinician profile"
    title="Jordan Ellis, LPC"
    intro="A direct, engaged therapist for adults who want to understand the sequence beneath a recurring problem—not simply manage its surface."
    crumbs={crumbs}
  />

  <section class="profile-intro">
    <div class="container profile-grid">
      <aside class="profile-card">
        <picture>
          <img
            src="/images/demo/clinician-placeholder.svg"
            width="700"
            height="780"
            loading="lazy"
            decoding="async"
            alt="Illustrated placeholder for fictional counselor Jordan Ellis"
          />
        </picture>

        <dl>
          <div><dt>Role</dt><dd>Individual counselor</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Clients</dt><dd>Adults</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Practice</dt><dd>Align Therapy Group</dd></div>
          <div><dt>Location</dt><dd>Madison, Wisconsin</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </aside>

      <div class="profile-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Working with Jordan</p>
        <h2>Warmth without vagueness. Structure without rigidity.</h2>

        <p>
          Jordan pays attention to the sequence around a problem: what happens
          first, what your mind predicts, what your body does, how you protect
          yourself, and what consequence follows. Making that sequence visible
          can create room for a response that fits the present more accurately.
        </p>

        <p>
          Her style is curious and active. She may reflect a pattern, ask a
          direct question, slow down around a body cue, or invite you to notice
          two conflicting reactions without immediately choosing between them.
        </p>

        <blockquote>
          “The goal is not to produce a better version of you for other people.
          It is to help you understand your own experience well enough to have
          more choice inside it.”
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="attention">
    <div class="container attention-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Questions Jordan listens for</p>
        <h2>The work often becomes clearer through better questions.</h2>
      </div>

      <ol>
        <li><span>01</span><p>What happens immediately before the familiar reaction?</p></li>
        <li><span>02</span><p>What does that reaction seem designed to prevent?</p></li>
        <li><span>03</span><p>Where does your body register the change first?</p></li>
        <li><span>04</span><p>What would become possible if you had five percent more choice?</p></li>
      </ol>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="method-profile">
    <div class="container method-grid">
      <div class="method-code">
        <span>02</span>
        <p>METHOD PROFILE</p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How Jordan may work</p>
        <h2>More than one framework, with a reason for using each.</h2>
        <p>
          Jordan may draw from Internal Family Systems, Somatic Experiencing,
          emotion- and attachment-focused work, present-moment awareness, and
          person-centered counseling.
        </p>
        <p>
          Methods are introduced in plain language and adjusted to the client.
          Insight, practical experimentation, relationship patterns, and body
          awareness may all have a place without every session needing to use
          every tool.
        </p>
        <a href="/approaches/">Review the approach map →</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="fit">
    <div class="container fit-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">A possible fit</p>
        <h2>You may appreciate Jordan’s style if you want therapy that is:</h2>
      </div>

      <ul>
        <li>Collaborative rather than prescriptive</li>
        <li>Direct without being confrontational</li>
        <li>Interested in both insight and real-life change</li>
        <li>Attentive to the body without treating it as the whole answer</li>
        <li>Flexible enough to question its own methods</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="demo-note">
    <div class="container note-grid">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Demonstration disclosure</p>
        <h2>This profile demonstrates presentation—not a real clinician’s credentials.</h2>
      </div>

      <div>
        <p>
          Jordan Ellis and Align Therapy Group are fictional. A real Brighter
          Sites clinician profile would use education, licensure, training,
          professional history, and service information supplied and verified
          by that clinician.
        </p>

        <div class="note-links">
          <a href="/services/">Explore services →</a>
          <a href="/contact/">View the contact experience →</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .profile-intro,
  .attention,
  .method-profile,
  .fit,
  .demo-note {
    padding: clamp(4rem,8vw,7rem) 0;
  }

  .profile-grid,
  .attention-grid,
  .method-grid,
  .fit-grid,
  .note-grid {
    display: grid;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .profile-card {
    align-self: start;
    border: 1px solid var(--sand);
    background: #f8fbff;
  }

  .profile-card picture {
    display: block;
    aspect-ratio: 4/5;
    overflow: hidden;
    background: #dce9f7;
  }

  .profile-card img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }

  .profile-card dl {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  .profile-card dl div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: .65rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sand);
  }

  .profile-card dt {
    color: #5f82ad;
    font-size: .65rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }

  .profile-card dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: .82rem;
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .profile-copy {
    align-self: center;
    max-width: 52rem;
  }

  blockquote {
    margin: 2rem 0 0;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    border-left: 4px solid #5f82ad;
    background: #edf4fb;
    color: var(--ink);
    font-size: 1.08rem;
    font-weight: 650;
  }

  .attention {
    background: #edf4fb;
  }

  .attention ol {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #bfcfe0;
    list-style: none;
  }

  .attention li {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 2.5rem 1fr;
    gap: 1rem;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #bfcfe0;
  }

  .attention li span {
    color: #5f82ad;
    font-size: .7rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .attention li p {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .method-profile {
    background: #0b1d3a;
    color: #dbe7f3;
  }

  .method-profile h2 {
    color: white;
  }

  .method-profile .eyebrow {
    color: #b5c8df;
  }

  .method-profile a {
    color: white;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .method-code {
    align-self: start;
    padding-top: .75rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.3);
  }

  .method-code span {
    color: #b5c8df;
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    font-weight: 800;
  }

  .method-code p {
    color: #aebed0;
    font-size: .68rem;
    font-weight: 800;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
  }

  .fit ul {
    display: grid;
    margin: 0;
    padding: 0;
    border-top: 1px solid var(--sand);
    list-style: none;
  }

  .fit li {
    padding: 1rem 0;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--sand);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-weight: 700;
  }

  .demo-note {
    background: #edf4fb;
  }

  .note-links {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 1rem 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
  }

  .note-links a {
    color: #3f648d;
    font-weight: 750;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  @media (min-width:48rem) {
    .profile-grid {
      grid-template-columns: minmax(16rem,.65fr) minmax(0,1.35fr);
      gap: clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);
    }

    .attention-grid,
    .fit-grid,
    .note-grid {
      grid-template-columns: .8fr 1.2fr;
      gap: clamp(3rem,7vw,7rem);
    }

    .method-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 12rem minmax(0,1fr);
      gap: clamp(3rem,7vw,8rem);
    }
  }
</style>
